<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Distance and displacement on a straight road</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Otieno rides a bicycle along a straight road that runs east to west. He rides \({@d1s@}\) km east from his home to the market, then \({@d2s@}\) km west to the posho mill.</p><p>(a) How far does he ride altogether?</p><div>[[input:ans1]] km [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) How far is the posho mill from his home?</p><div>[[input:ans2]] km [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) In which direction is the posho mill from his home?</p><div>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Draw the road with home at the start. The first ride goes \({@d1s@}\) km east; the second comes back \({@d2s@}\) km west.</p><p>(a) The distance ridden counts every kilometre: \({@d1s@} + {@d2s@} = {@dists@}\) km.</p><p>(b) The displacement is where he ends up compared with where he started, in a straight line. [[if test="ise"]]He came back less than he went, so he ends \({@d1s@} - {@d2s@} = {@disps@}\) km from home.[[else]]He came back further than he went, so he ends \({@d2s@} - {@d1s@} = {@disps@}\) km from home, on the other side.[[/if]]</p><p>(c) [[if test="ise"]]East of home: the ride east was the longer one.[[else]]West of home: the ride west was the longer one.[[/if]] Distance is a scalar; displacement, a size together with a direction, is a vector.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* exd: shortest exact decimal display of a terminating value (up to 3 d.p.) */
exd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else if integerp(10*v) then dispdp(float(v),1) else if integerp(100*v) then dispdp(float(v),2) else dispdp(float(v),3);
/* Design: distance and displacement on a straight road. 5 east and 5 west endings; d1, d2, d1 + d2 and |d1 - d2| are distinct on every entry. Source: original. */
dl: [[5,8],[7,5],[9/2,15/2],[13/2,5/2],[4,3],[3/2,9/2],[5,7/2],[3,7],[7,5/2],[9/2,6]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
d1: dl[ix][1]; d2: dl[ix][2];
dist: d1+d2; disp: abs(d1-d2);
ise: is(d2<d1);
d1s: exd(d1); d2s: exd(d2); dists: exd(dist); disps: exd(disp);
opt3: [["east", ise, "east"], ["west", not ise, "west"]];
ta3: first(mcq_correct(opt3));
wr3: if ise then "west" else "east";
mdisp: -disp; g1: dist+1; g2: disp+1;
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
